WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.080
SCP-682 Vs SCP-938.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.240
Can this electrical entity provide an adequate
shock to 682’s system?

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.480
SCP-682 was placed in a containment chamber
attached to Site-07.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.880
An electric device was brought into the room
and routed into SCP-938.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.080
The device increased in electrical voltage
to the point that it damaged SCP-682, causing

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.960
burns to its body and paralyzing it for one
hour.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.200
At this point, it regained motion capabilities
and shot electricity from its spine through

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.920
its head.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.840
Then, it lost consciousness - though it was
still breathing - and remained that way for

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.920
several days as its body recovered.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.520
Not quite as electrifying as the Foundation
had hoped, so it appeared.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.240
The researcher for this test, Dr. Carly, did
at least note that electrical or mind-based

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.560
SCPs did tend to keep SCP-682 immobilized
longer than physical or chemical attacks.

